ns probe-1bvi-w

def ov := @[{:a {:b {:x 1}}}]

;; 1b-vi-D-1 finding: under a TOTAL collapse, what does an ORDINAL branch head do?
;; (1) the caret collapse family through the `(@ord N)` head
ov{0.a.b.x^-}
ov{0.a.b^-}
ov{0.a.b.x^-_}
;; (2) no collapse — the head's own landing (keyless component over the element)
ov{0.a.b.x}
ov{0.a^.b^.x}
;; (3) the star family today: `*` and the C-injected `*-`'s equivalent
ov{0.a.b*}
ov{0.a^.b*}
;; (4) is the ordinal head itself dissolvable? (Q_T4a's ordinal-`^` shapes)
ov{0^.a.b.x}
ov{0^.a^.b*}
